  normative VM steps; hostile argument mutations and multiplication reject.
  A separate byte `0x40` attempt reached the backend and refused its missing
  positional witness. The original Fibonacci loop, dynamic guest arithmetic
  and full P0 acceptance are still pending.
- The source-proven masked-sum probe reproduces the original loop's
  `(a + b) & 255U` arithmetic with a `u32` intermediate 377 before
  truncation by `& 255U`. Its pinned JSON adapter proof now supports
  nested parentheses and explicit `putchar((int)next)` casts. Opposite
  constant branches compile to actual guest bytes `0x41`/`0x42` in
  31/69 normative VM steps; altered ancestry and unsupported effects reject.
  Guest arithmetic, the full Fibonacci loop and P0 completion remain pending.
- A source-proven zero-based `for` loop with up to twelve iterations now
  folds closed, output-free C state updates including an iteration-local
  declaration, source-checked conditional and Fibonacci-style transfers.
  An eight-iteration variant independently computes `b=42`, then emits
  `0x41` after XOR 107 in 31 normative VM steps; a seven-iteration variant
